<title>JAPAN: DKB says has no objection to MOF penalties.</title>
<headline>DKB says has no objection to MOF penalties.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd has no objections to measures to be taken against the bank by the Ministry of Finance (MOF) for its alleged involvement in a racketeer payoff scandal, DKB president Katsuyuki Sugita told reporters on Wednesday after meeting the ministry's banking bureau chief.  </p>
<p>He said the bank would accept the measures sincerely.</p>
<p>&quot;We will take the measures sincerely,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Asked whether the bank had objected to the MOF's planned penalties, which it was told of earlier this week, he said: &quot;No.&quot;</p>
</text>
